5. Conclusion and future work
Phishing email is one of the fastest-growing cybercrimes on the Internet, and it affects businesses and individuals alike. It also costs billions of dollars every year. Phishing methods are rapidly changing and depend on the intelligence of the hacker. Therefore, taking advantage of machine deep learning to compete and match human intelligence is a perfect solution.
The main aim of this study is to propose a solution that improves the performance and accuracy of phishing email classification and detection. It examined a phishing email detection classification model using NLP and a deep learning algorithm based on GCN. The model was tested with a supervised learning approach and was proved to improve classification accuracy and performance in comparison to other deep learning methods with a short time for training and a high true positive rate, true negative rate, hight recall, precision, f-measure, and overall accuracy.
It highlights the significance of examining the text features of an email body to detect phishing because the text features are a new research direction in the email phishing detection area, with only a few studies focusing on the email’s body text. This research was among the first, to the best of our knowledge, to examine the use of the GCN algorithm in detecting phishing in the email body text. This will lead to more investigation in the field of phishing detection in text, whether in emails, social media messages, or even phishing websites.

Furthermore, we plan to conduct a future study using a nonEnglish corpus. In addition, because the solution’s concept depends on text classification, we assume it can be applied to email categorisation tasks.
Moreover, the proposed detection classifier can accurately detect phishing emails based on body text that has not been seen before, so we assume its effectiveness in detecting zeroday phishing attacks. Hence, further investigation will be done to evaluate its effectiveness in detecting zero-day phishing emails that have been spreading widely recently.
